          "score": 5,
          "excerpts": [
            {
              "line": 71,
              "text": "AIL Operational Execution exists because standard LLM reasoning is confirmatory: models optimize for coherence, not falsification. The inversion step forces a model to defend the opposite of its first instinct, exposing hidden assumptions and weak evidence chains. Delta scoring converts this qualitative exercise into a quantitative signal. The complexity budget prevents runaway multi-model orchestration."
            },
            {
              "line": 130,
              "text": "- [ ] Inversion crew invoked with rule-based prompts (not free-form)"
            },
            {
              "line": 17,
              "text": "AIL Operational Execution operationalizes Axiom Inversion Logic (AIL) as a 5-stage pipeline (Identify \u2192 Invert \u2192 Re-Derive \u2192 Compare \u2192 Synthesize) with rule-based Multi-Operator Inverse Epistemic (MoIE) routing. The playbook specifies mode-based execution (Mode A for single-operator tasks, Mode B for multi-operator inversions), delta scoring thresholds (0.4/0.7), SHA-256 deduplication, and complexity budgets. The runtime contract is defined via `mission.json`, `stage_gate.json`, and `ail_runs.db` schemas."
            },
